%% DOC-03 — State diagram: reconciliation run and period lifecycle (one account, one month)
%% State names are the run status values used in the database. Every transition writes an audit event (CR-08).
    direction TB
    [*] --> created: run started (UC-01)
    created --> validating: files imported
    validating --> validation_failed: file-level check fails (CR-17)
    validation_failed --> validating: corrected file re-imported
    validating --> processing: all file-level checks pass
    processing --> in_review: matching, scoring and routing complete
    in_review --> ready_to_close: all decided, package generated, chain verified
    ready_to_close --> in_review: decision changed or gap found
    ready_to_close --> closed: Controller signs off, CR-05, CR-10, lock event
    closed --> reopen_requested: ROL-01 or ROL-02 requests, reason required
    reopen_requested --> closed: request rejected
    reopen_requested --> in_review: Controller approves, CR-06
    closed --> [*]

    note right of closed
        Locked: no imports, decisions
        or adjustments (FR-PER-03).
        Chain-head hash printed on
        the signed summary (FR-AUD-07)
    end note
    note left of in_review
        After reopening, a new sign-off
        is required to close again (FR-PER-05)
    end note
